For those planning to take the Claude Certified Architect – Foundations certification, below are some recommendations for exam registration and preparation based on my experience.
1. Exam Registration
Go to the Anthropic Partner Skilljar portal:
Anthropic Partner Academy
Navigate to:
Certification → Claude Certified Architect – Foundations → Register for Exam
I would recommend taking the exam at a test center, if feasible. I have heard of cases where candidates taking the exam from home faced network/disconnection issues.
Also, please note that you cannot take the exam using an Altimetrik laptop, so plan accordingly if you choose the online/proctored option.
2. Exam Preparation
Anthropic provides certification preparation courses through Skilljar:
Claude Certification Exam Prep Courses
I recommend completing the courses relevant to the Claude Certified Architect – Foundations exam.
The exam guide attached contains the syllabus and exam domains. For my preparation, I used the exam guide as the syllabus, provided it to Claude as context, and studied each topic/domain systematically. This worked well for me.
3. Mock Tests / Practice Questions
I don't currently see an official mock test available in the Skilljar portal. However, there are a few other options:
Udemy
Udemy has mock tests for this certification. If you don't have Udemy access, contact Rimpa Kundu and mention that you need access for certification preparation.
CertSafari
CertSafari: Explore Freely
This site provides around 300 practice questions — 60 questions for each domain. I found this useful for preparation and assessing coverage across the syllabus.
There are also some additional mock exams available online:
https://claudecertificationguide.com/mock-exam
https://ccaf.cyberskill.world/practice
I haven't personally tried these two, so please use them as supplementary practice resources rather than relying on them as authoritative exam material.
Suggested Preparation Approach
Review the official exam guide and understand all syllabus domains.
Complete the corresponding Skilljar preparation courses.
Study each syllabus topic systematically using Claude and the official learning material.
Practice domain-wise questions to identify weaker areas.
Get some hands-on experience with Claude using use cases from your strongest business domain.
Revise those areas before attempting full mock exams.
Prefer a test center for the actual exam 
All the best for your preparation and certification!!!
